+### `withoutQuery(input, keys?)`
+
+Removes the complete query, or only fields with the supplied decoded keys, from a URL.
+
+When removing selected keys, the retained query fields are not decoded or reserialized, so their original spelling, values, percent-escape casing, order, and separators are preserved. An empty key list or a query without matching keys returns the input unchanged.
+
+**Example:**
+
+```js
+withoutQuery("/foo?bar=1&baz=2#hash"); // "/foo#hash"
+withoutQuery("/foo?bar=1&baz=2", "bar"); // "/foo?baz=2"
+```
+
 ### `withoutTrailingSlash(input, respectQueryAndFragment?)`
 
 Removes the trailing slash from the URL or pathname.
